<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Víctor Paz Estenssoro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1907">1907</a>–<a href="/years/2001">2001</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Víctor Paz Estenssoro was a Bolivian statesman who founded the Revolutionary Nationalist Movement (MNR) and served as president four times. Leading the 1952 revolution, he introduced universal suffrage, nationalised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> mines and began land reform. The military overthrew him in 1964. In his last term, from 1985 to 1989, he ended hyperinflation with a harsh free-market stabilisation programme.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victor-paz-estenssoro.jpg" alt="Víctor Paz Estenssoro" width="320" height="516" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author, Carlos Mesa collection, La Paz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V%C3%ADctor_Paz_Estenssoro_(1964)_(Non-Sepia).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
